@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<section class="hero">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">For job seekers who prepare with AI</p>
    <h1>JobHunt HQ</h1>
    <p class="pitch">Track every application. Prepare with your own AI. Apply as yourself.</p>
    <p class="hero-sub">
        One calm workspace for your whole job search — check every posting against
        your own criteria, export a fact-locked AI packet for the assistant you already
        use, and track every follow-up across your pipeline.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Dashboard">Open my dashboard</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/Register">Create an account</a>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="trust-callout" aria-label="Core product promise">
    <strong>The never-submit rule:</strong> JobHunt HQ never submits an application for you, never logs into job boards or employer sites as you, and never invents experience. It prepares and visualizes — you review and press submit yourself.
</section>

<section class="workflow-section">
    <h2>How a posting becomes a prepared application</h2>
    <div class="workflow-grid">
        <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">1</span>
            <h3>Set your criteria once</h3>
            <p>Save your target roles, pay floor, must-haves, deal-breakers, skip companies, and standing answers in your search profile.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">2</span>
            <h3>Capture &amp; check fit</h3>
            <p>Paste a posting or fetch it from its URL. A deterministic rule check scores the match (<span class="status-pill fit-pill fit-strong-fit">Strong fit</span>, <span class="status-pill fit-pill fit-possible">Possible</span>, <span class="status-pill fit-pill fit-blocked">Blocked</span>) and explains every point.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">3</span>
            <h3>Hand the packet to your AI</h3>
            <p>Download or copy a self-contained AI packet (.md or .json) containing the posting, fit reasons, standing answers, ATS form guide, and your resume text — wrapped in strict fact-only instructions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">4</span>
            <h3>Review, apply &amp; follow up</h3>
            <p>Submit the application yourself, record the resume used and next action due date, and drag the card across your pipeline board.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pipeline-section">
    <h2>Your search, as a pipeline</h2>
    <p>
        Every opportunity moves through the same five active stages, so you always know
        where things stand and what needs your attention next.
    </p>
    <ol class="pipeline">
        <li class="stage stage-saved">Saved</li>
        <li class="stage stage-applied">Applied</li>
        <li class="stage stage-screening">Screening</li>
        <li class="stage stage-interview">Interview</li>
        <li class="stage stage-final">Offer</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="pipeline-note">
        Roles that don't work out land in Rejected, Ghosted, or Withdrawn — out of
        the way, but never lost.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="features-section">
    <h2>Everything in one place</h2>
    <div class="features">
        <div class="feature">
            <h3>Deterministic fit checks</h3>
            <p>Every rule is transparent: skip lists, deal-breakers, pay floor comparisons, and a must-have keyword checklist.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
            <h3>Bring-your-own-AI packets</h3>
            <p>Works with ChatGPT, Claude, or any assistant you trust — with ATS-specific guidance for Workday, Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workable, and iCIMS.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
            <h3>The right resume, every time</h3>
            <p>Store resume PDFs privately in Azure Blob Storage, record which version went where, and automatically embed extracted text into packets.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
            <h3>Next actions, not noise</h3>
            <p>Each application carries a next action and due date, surfaced on your dashboard, board cards, and daily email digest.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="status-section">
    <h2>Project milestones</h2>
    <ul class="status-list">
        <li>
            <span class="status-badge status-done">Done</span>
            <strong>M1 — Azure foundation.</strong>
            Live on Azure App Service with continuous deployment from GitHub.
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="status-badge status-done">Done</span>
            <strong>M2 — Core pipeline &amp; tracker.</strong>
            Account isolation, full application CRUD, status pipeline, dashboard, and CSV import.
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="status-badge status-done">Done</span>
            <strong>M3 — Cloud-native storage &amp; telemetry.</strong>
            Private resume PDF uploads in Blob Storage, daily follow-up digest Function, Key Vault secrets, and Application Insights.
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="status-badge status-active">Live</span>
            <strong>M4 — Search profile, fit checks, pipeline board &amp; AI packets.</strong>
            Deterministic fit scoring, SSRF-guarded URL fetching, interactive Kanban board, and v2 Markdown/JSON AI packets.
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>
